-- title:
--   Divisor presenting the dual of an invertible ideal sheaf
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field and $x\colon X\to\operatorname{Spec}K$ a morphism with $X$ integral and $x$ separated, quasi-compact and smooth of relative dimension one, and let $I$ be an ideal sheaf datum on $X$ which is invertible in the sense that every point of $X$ lies in some $X.\mathrm{basicOpen}\,f$, with $f\in\Gamma(X,U)$ for an affine open $U$, such that $I$ on the affine basic open of $f$ is generated by a single non-zero-divisor. Regard $K(X)=X.\mathrm{functionField}$ as a $K$-algebra through [`AlgebraicCurve.baseToFunctionField x`](def/AlgebraicCurve_CurveModel.html#L18). Then there are a divisor $D$, i.e. a finitely supported $\mathbb Z$-valued function on the places of $K(X)/K$ (valuation subrings of $K(X)$, proper, containing $K$ and principal ideal rings), and additive maps $\varphi_U\colon\Gamma(I.\mathrm{invModule},U)\to K(X)$ for all opens $U$, where $I.\mathrm{invModule}$ is the dual of the $\mathcal O_X$-module $I.\mathrm{module}$, with the following properties. The $\varphi_U$ are compatible with restriction along $V\le U$ whenever $V$ is nonempty; $\varphi_U(a\cdot m)=\mathrm{algebraMap}(a)\,\varphi_U(m)$ for nonempty $U$, $a\in\Gamma(X,U)$; $\varphi_U$ is injective for nonempty $U$; for nonempty affine $U$ the image of $\varphi_U$ is the $K$-submodule $\{h:\ v(h)\le\exp(D v)\ \text{for all } v\in S_U\}$, where $S_U=\mathrm{placesOf}\,x\,U$ consists of the places $v$ for which the image of the stalk $\mathcal O_{X,y}$ in $K(X)$ is the valuation subring of $v$ for some closed point $y\in U$; and if $s\in\Gamma(I.\mathrm{invModule},U)$ and $y\in U$ is a closed point such that on every open $W\le U$ containing $y$ each section of $I.\mathrm{invModule}$ is a multiple of $s|_W$, then $\exp(D v)=v(\varphi_U(s))$ for every place $v$ centred at $y$. Moreover the element $f:=\varphi_\top$ of the canonical section, the image under $I.\mathrm{invModuleSection}$ (the transpose of $I.\mathrm{moduleι}$) of the unit section $1$ over $\top$, is nonzero, and for every affine open $U$, every $g\in\Gamma(X,U)$ and closed point $y\in U$ with $I$ on $U$ equal to the ideal generated by $g$, and every place $v$ centred at $y$, one has $D v+\operatorname{ord}_v(f)=\operatorname{ord}_v(g)$, where $\operatorname{ord}_v(h)=-\log v(h)$.
--
--   This is the statement, for a smooth curve over a field, that the invertible sheaf $\mathcal O_X(Z)=\mathcal I^{-1}$ attached to an effective Cartier divisor $Z$ with ideal $\mathcal I$ admits a presentation inside the function field by Riemann–Roch spaces, its divisor being the Weil divisor of $Z$ shifted by the divisor of the rational function attached to the canonical section; it is the counterpart for the dual of the corresponding statement for the ideal sheaf itself. It feeds the computation of divisor classes used by [`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.isPrincipal_sub_single_of_presentation_ker_pow`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.isPrincipal_sub_single_of_presentation_ker_pow).
